## AI Agents
# Specify when AI Agents, LLMs or similar where used to create parts or the whole commit.
# When using JetBrains Junie with default settings, uncomment the two lines below.
#
#AI-Agent: JetBrains Junie (@junie-agent)
#AI-Model: Google Gemini 3 Flash (gemini-3-flash-preview)
#
# Otherwise, fill the following in and uncomment them:
#
#AI-Agent: Company Product (Optional-Marketing)
#AI-Model: Company Model Version (model-api-identifier)
#
# Why AI-Agent?
# This allows others to know and understand what tool you used.
# If you use Claude Code, the text "Anthropic Claude Code (@claude)" lets others know that.
# Example for OpenCode: "Anomaly OpenCode (@opencode-agent[bot])".
#
# Why AI-Model?
# Since nearly every Agent supports multiple models and each model behaving differently,
# knowing the model becomes imporant. The API Identifier helps others select the same model.
# If you use Sonnet 4.6, the text "Anthropic Claude Sonnet 4.6 (claude-sonnet-4-6)" gives that information.
# Example for Gemini 3: "Google Gemini 3 Flash (gemini-3-flash-preview)"
#
# Do NOT include the Agent via an "Co-Authored-By".
# That one should be reserved for human co-authors, not tools/programs/LLMs.
